/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  thermoPhysPropDict (v2) -- gamma-phi, predictive UNIFAC liquid, SRK vapour.

  The MTBE system: methanol, isobutene, MTBE and the C4 cut.  Methanol is the
  strongly non-ideal member (it forms azeotropes with the C4 hydrocarbons and
  with MTBE), so the liquid is the predictive group-contribution UNIFAC; the
  Raoult datum (gamma -> 1 as x -> 1) is the standard state the reaction's K_a
  is written in.  The vapour at 7 bar is a REAL gas, SRK (kij = 0, announced): under an ideal
  vapour the latent heat the column prices at its 400 K reboiler is about
  1.3 kJ/mol too high (the vapour's departure, H_res of 1.34 kJ/mol at 7 bar,
  is missing), which is most of the gap to the case this one is measured
  against, whose vapour is a Redlich-Kwong equation of state.  SRK is
  Choupo's cubic of that family.  The pure-liquid reference carries phi_sat
  and Poynting (a real vapour counted on both sides of K), so the
  temperatures hold as well as the duties.

  C256 (2026-11-09), MEASURED: propane (Tc 369.8 K) is priced through a vapour
  pressure continued past Tc on the hottest stages (the reboiler at 400.7 K),
  where it is a trace (1e-6 of the bottoms), so no printed number moves with
  that K at golden tolerance.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

recordType    thermophysicalPropertySystem;
schemaVersion 2;

components ( methanol  isoButene  methylTertButylEther  propane  isoButane
             nButane  1Butene  cis2Butene  trans2Butene );

equilibrium
{
    formulation gammaPhi;

    liquid
    {
        activityModel { model UNIFAC; }
        standardState pureLiquid;
    }

    vapour
    {
        fugacityModel SRK;
    }
}
